// folder structure of nuxt

.nuxt/: A generated folder used by Nuxt to store build artifacts. Do not edit this manually.

assets/: Contains uncompiled files like SCSS, CSS, and images that you want processed by Vite or Webpack.

public/: Stores static files served at the root URL (e.g., favicon.ico, robots.txt). These are not processed by the build tool.

components/: All Vue components go here. Nuxt auto-imports these, so you can use them in your templates without manual import statements.

pages/: Enables file-system routing. Every .vue file here automatically becomes a URL route.

layouts/: Used for reusable page structures (e.g., a default.vue containing your Navbar and Footer).

server/: Used for backend logic. Subfolders include api/ (for REST endpoints), routes/, and middleware/.

composables/: Dedicated for Vue Composition API functions. Nuxt auto-imports these globally.

middleware/: Contains route guards to run code before navigating to a specific page.

plugins/: Used to run code before the Vue app is instantiated (e.g., initializing an analytics tool).

utils/: For helper functions and utility logic; also benefits from auto-imports.

// Running nuxt app

Development

- `npm run dev`

Cleaning & Fixes

- `npx nuxi clean`

Production

- `npm run build`
